#. module: hrm_data_import
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:hrm_data_import.monthly_manual_help
msgid ""
"<strong>Check and calculate payroll.</strong><br/>\n"
"              Click <strong>Refresh monthly data</strong>. Check paid days, performance, contract salary and each employee status. Open <strong>Set up payroll period</strong> and <strong>3. Check data</strong> to find missing information.<br/>\n"
"              Select an employee or leave blank for all, then click <strong>Quick payroll calculation</strong>. Resolve missing contracts, attendance or performance first. Base salary comes from the contract. Employee insurance reduces net pay; employer insurance is shown separately."
msgstr ""

#. module: hrm_data_import
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:hrm_data_import.monthly_manual_help
msgid ""
"<strong>Correct data and review history.</strong><br/>\n"
"              Before calculation: create a new manual entry with the same source ID, date/component and a higher revision (2, 3, etc.). Enter the reason. Saved entries cannot be edited directly. Correct Excel inputs through their original Excel source and revision.<br/>\n"
"              After calculation: open <strong>Set up payroll period</strong>, enter a reopening reason and click <strong>Reopen for correction and recalculation</strong>. Save the correction and run <strong>Quick payroll calculation</strong>. To replace a component amount, open the payslip and <strong>Adjust salary</strong>, enter the replacement and reason, approve it, then recalculate.<br/>\n"
"              To change a formula: Payslip → <strong>Excel formulas</strong> → Create new version → select effective dates → Test → Approve version. Approved/finalized periods are locked. Do not overwrite issued payslips.<br/>\n"
"              Change Year/Month to review history. Open <strong>Attendance / performance</strong> on the employee row to inspect sources and import batch logs, or use <strong>Import and payroll logs</strong>."
msgstr ""

#. module: hrm_data_import
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:hrm_data_import.monthly_manual_help
msgid ""
"<strong>Create a period if the month has none.</strong><br/>\n"
"              Click <strong>Set up payroll period</strong>. Check the first/last date of the month, standard working days, hours per day and the correct regional minimum wage for unemployment insurance. Save, return and click <strong>Refresh monthly data</strong>. Reuse an existing period instead of creating a duplicate.<br/>\n"
"              Employees need an active contract, salary structure and base salary. Use a new contract/addendum for lasting contract changes; do not re-enter base salary every month."
msgstr ""

#. module: hrm_data_import
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:hrm_data_import.monthly_manual_help
msgid ""
"<strong>Enter performance, bonuses or salary components.</strong><br/>\n"
"              Click <strong>Manual entry / attendance</strong>, select <strong>Performance</strong> or <strong>Salary component</strong>, choose a component in the contract salary structure and enter the amount. Use a stable employee/component/month source ID such as <code>NV001-202611-KPI</code>, revision 1 and an approval reason.<br/>\n"
"              Click <strong>Validate and save</strong> and review the results/log. If performance is required and a zero amount is confirmed, enter 0 for the appropriate component. Do not re-enter Excel amounts through a separate web source; this can conflict or double-count."
msgstr ""

#. module: hrm_data_import
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:hrm_data_import.monthly_manual_help
msgid ""
"<strong>Example: November 2026.</strong> Use confirmed November attendance "
"and amounts. A new month does not automatically copy the previous month "
"attendance, bonuses or payroll."
msgstr ""

#. module: hrm_data_import
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:hrm_data_import.monthly_manual_help
msgid ""
"<strong>Record daily attendance.</strong><br/>\n"
"              Click <strong>Manual entry / attendance</strong>, check the company, period and employee, select <strong>Attendance</strong>, then enter the work date and hours. For example, enter 8 for eight hours on 02/11/2026. Use 0 only for confirmed zero hours, not for unknown data.<br/>\n"
"              Use a stable employee-and-date source ID such as <code>NV001-20261102</code>. Start at revision <strong>1</strong>. Enter an approval reference / correction reason, then click <strong>Validate and save</strong>. Confirm the batch is <strong>Saved</strong>; review rejected rows and logs before continuing.<br/>\n"
"              Repeat for each date and employee. Return to <strong>Refresh monthly data</strong>, then <strong>Attendance grid, days 01–31</strong> to review the month."
msgstr ""

#. module: hrm_data_import
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:hrm_data_import.monthly_manual_help
msgid ""
"<strong>Review payslips and download Excel.</strong><br/>\n"
"              Click <strong>Refresh monthly data</strong> after calculation. Open each <strong>Payslip</strong> or <strong>Excel-style payroll</strong> to check components, insurance, deductions and net pay. Click <strong>Export payroll Excel</strong> for the selected month. A selected employee limits this export to that person; clear the employee to export the company.<br/>\n"
"              The <strong>Export entire month to Excel</strong> button on the 52-column grid or payslip always exports the whole month."
msgstr ""

#. module: hrm_data_import
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:hrm_data_import.monthly_manual_help
msgid ""
"<strong>Select the month and employees.</strong><br/>\n"
"              Select Company, Year and Month above. Leave Employee blank for the whole company or select one employee. Click <strong>Refresh monthly data</strong> after changing filters."
msgstr ""

#. module: hrm_data_import
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:hrm_data_import.monthly_manual_help
msgid ""
"<strong>Start a new payroll month:</strong> select year/month → Set up "
"payroll period → Manual entry / attendance → Quick payroll calculation."
msgstr ""

